## What we get

When someone types:

```text
/HO
```

the bot will respond with something like:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HANDOVER UPDATE                     │
│ Current production handover status  │
│                                     │
│ REPORTING DATE              01-Sep │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🔴 SHOW STOPPER / HIGH PRIORITY     │
│ PRB015455 - OCCW                    │
│ ...                                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🟠 PRBs LINKED WITH CURRENT DAY     │
│ 3AT20.01 | FIC | ...                │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🔵 RITM                             │
│ RITM1878290 - Please work on this   │
│ RITM1873466 - Please work on this   │
│ ...                                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🟡 PROBLEMS                         │
│ ...                                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 🟣 CTASKS                           │
│ ...                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

And the **big advantage** is:

**User updates original HO sheet → formulas update `HO_Automation` → `/HO` reads `HO_Automation` → Teams always shows latest HO.**

No Power Automate is involved in the Excel update itself. Power Automate only **reads the prepared table**.

